{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@preconcurrency","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"unfolding","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"produce"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:Scs7Elementxmfp","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Error"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"produce","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A closure that asynchronously produces elements for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stream."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this convenience initializer when you have an asynchronous function"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that can produce elements for the stream, and don’t want to invoke","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a continuation manually. This initializer “unfolds” your closure into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a full-blown asynchronous stream. The created stream handles adherence to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol automatically. To terminate the stream with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an error, throw the error from your closure."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example shows an "},{"code":"AsyncThrowingStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" created with this"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"initializer that produces random numbers on a one-second interval. If the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random number is divisible by 5 with no remainder, the stream throws a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MyRandomNumberError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let stream = AsyncThrowingStream<Int, Error> {","    await Task.sleep(1 * 1_000_000_000)","    let random = Int.random(in: 1...10)","    if random % 5 == 0 {","        throw MyRandomNumberError()","    }","    return random","}","","\/\/ Call point:","do {","    for try await random in stream {","        print(random)","    }","} catch {","    print(error)","}"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Constructs an asynchronous throwing stream from a given element-producing","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"init","title":"init(unfolding:)","externalID":"s:Scs9unfoldingScsyxs5Error_pGxSgyYaKc_tcsAB_pRs_rlufc","roleHeading":"Initializer","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"unfolding"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"kind":"text","text":" () "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Scs7Elementxmfp","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text"